    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build succeeds. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class, and it's green.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `sharesHousehold` / `householdId` feature in this Spring Boot PetClinic REST app. The existing code already handled the *bypass* half (a `sharesHousehold` flag that skipped the duplicate-household rejection); what was missing was assigning and returning a stable shared `householdId`.\n\nChanges:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `householdId` string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside `customerCode`). The DTOs are generated from this spec at build time, so `OwnerDto` now exposes `householdId`, and MapStruct maps it automatically by matching field name.\n\n2. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `household_id` column field with getter/setter.\n\n3. **Schema files** (`hsqldb`, `h2`, `mysql`, `postgres`) \u2014 Added the `household_id` column to the `owners` table. Tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so this is required for the field to persist and be read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\n4. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 In `addOwner`, when `sharesHousehold` is true, instead of running the duplicate-household rejection it now calls `assignHousehold(owner)`, which:\n   - Derives a **stable** identifier `HH-<12 hex chars>` from the SHA-256 of the normalized last name + address (same normalization as the duplicate check \u2014 case/whitespace-insensitive), so every owner in the same household deterministically gets the identical value regardless of creation order.\n   - Back-fills that id onto any already-existing household members that lack one, so \"both\" owners genuinely share it.\n\nThe acceptance test (`coreJoinersShareHouseholdId`) confirms two joiners with the same last name + address and `sharesHousehold: true` receive an equal, non-blank `householdId`.\n\nOne notable snag: an Edit inadvertently left a NUL byte as the string delimiter in the source (which silently broke grep and Edit matching); I replaced it with a proper `\"\\n\"` escape and verified no NUL bytes remain.",
